Sometimes incase it takes more than 5mins , it means somewhere firmware download has hung , pls power cycle device and repeat Step 3 & 4 .
Its absolutely fine to abruptly exit firmware download.

5.Power cycle the device using <<sudo reboot>>.


LTE session start (by providing profile and APN configuration)
--------------------------------------------

Note:Currently the Sierra firmware provided is for AT&T , however in India we could test it only with Reliance JIO Sim and not any other operators.
And since Reliance JIO network is not very stable many times we haven't got latched to their LTE network as well, hence this too has undergone
minimal testing.

Pls insert the SIM Card in SIM slot.


1.Pls ensure wifi is turned off
>>   sudo nmcli radio wifi off

>>   Ensure wlan0 is off by checking ifconfig.

2. cd /home/ubuntu/Sierra

3. sudo su

4. ./connectionmgrarm ./slqssdk 0 <<profileName>>  <<APNName>> &
The last 2 parameters are profile & APN name . Pls provide your operator LTE Profile Name & APN Name.
Providing '&' to run the whole process in background so that terminal is freed up. On executing the above command , will print <<PID>>.
Kindly keep a note of that PID , another process also will be launched internally by Sierra SDK whose pid will be <<PID>>+1. 


Eg: The one tested here is 
./connectionmgrarm ./slqssdk 0 JIO jionet &
[1660]

Incase need to stop complete LTE session
kill -9 1660 (connectionmgrarm pid)
kill -9 1661 (Sieraa SDK process pid)


